# r1111 rerun of b2_short_timers.qb rows SQ-WO-27 (BATCH-FAULT fixes, scratch_run_2026-11-11.md)
# r1109wo boot A2: sleepDurationSeconds, angerDurationSeconds, angrySleepDurationSeconds = 5; chance 100, threshold 75.
# randomTickSpeed 0 throughout, except the window in SQ-WO-14. Deviations from the queue text, scratch-only:
# timer rows run at pace 0.2 (at 2 s per command the 5 s timers expire before they are read);
# SQ-WO-14 opens a short random-tick window then reads at once (a 5 s tired sleep inside a 90 s wait is usually over);
# SQ-WO-18 and the angry case of -28 make the tree angry by waking a sleeper, so it has a real timer (a bare [state=angry] has none and sleeps within 23 ticks);
# SQ-WO-28 uses one Z per case (a fresh tree, no leftover blow or cooldown).
pace 1

## SETUP-A2 | forceload, bots
> forceload add 270 290 900 320
sleep 8
> pbot spawn G 280 -60 280 minecraft:overworld survival
> pbot spawn H 276 -60 280 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 0
> weather clear
> time set noon

